      },
      {
        "id": "notes-1",
        "type": "notes",
        "name": "Info",
        "position": { "x": 0, "y": 3 },
        "params": {
          "text": "SAMPLER — LOAD YOUR OWN\n\nA pitched one-shot .wav player. No sample is bundled — load your own.\n\n1. Click 'Load .wav' on the Sampler and pick a short file (a drum hit, a vocal phrase, a synth stab). It is decoded, mono-mixed and resampled to the engine rate.\n2. Press Play. The Step Sequencer fires the Sampler's Trigger on each active step (a 16-step groove with gaps + velocity accents).\n3. 'Preview' auditions the loaded file locally without the engine.\n\nSignal: Step Sequencer (gate) -> Sampler -> Reverb -> Output\n\nTIPS\n- All step pitches are 0, so any percussion sample plays untransposed. Edit the step pitches (relative semitones) to play a MELODY — the sequencer's CV is patched to the Sampler's Pitch input (V/oct, +12 = one octave up).\n- Switch the Sampler to Loop mode for sustained, droning textures.\n- Pitch / Level / Attack / Release knobs shape each hit; short Release = tight, long Release = a tail.\n\nLICENSE: commercial packs (e.g. AudioRealism 909) are usable but NOT redistributable — load them locally, don't commit them. CC0 / public-domain samples can be bundled later."
        }
      }
    ],
    "connections": [
      {
        "from": { "moduleId": "seq-1", "portId": "gate-out" },
        "to": { "moduleId": "sampler-1", "portId": "trigger" },
        "kind": "gate"
      },
      {
        "from": { "moduleId": "seq-1", "portId": "cv-out" },
        "to": { "moduleId": "sampler-1", "portId": "pitch" },
        "kind": "cv"
      },
      {
        "from": { "moduleId": "sampler-1", "portId": "out" },
        "to": { "moduleId": "reverb-1", "portId": "in" },
        "kind": "audio"
      },
      {
        "from": { "moduleId": "reverb-1", "portId": "out" },
        "to": { "moduleId": "out-1", "portId": "in" },
        "kind": "audio"
      }
    ]
  }
